From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 13:13:42 +0200
Subject: net: dsa: lantiq: add the GSWIP 3.0 parser microcode

The classification engine's parser runs from a 256-row table that has to be
written before the switch classifies anything, and this generation's table is
not the GSWIP-2.x one: the output-field and protocol-flag numbers the rows
refer to are renumbered, so the two tables are carried and named apart.

Add the table and load it. The load has an ordering this generation needs and
the common function library's shared version does not express: the macro's
global enable is set before the microcode is marked invalid, and the per-port
fetch and store engines are held off across the write. It also has to happen
before the integrated PHYs are started, which is earlier than setup() runs,
so the model loads it from probe and the shared version repeats it after the
reset in setup().

Two more pieces of this generation's bring-up come with it. The queue
manager's drop-policy selector is two bits wide here rather than one and is
run at zero. Source-address spoofing detection on the CPU port, which the
vendor driver turns on, is deliberately left off: it drops a frame whose
source address the switch has learned on another port, and that is exactly
what the software bridge sends whenever it forwards on the switch's behalf.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

